Chapter: PathReal

  cites Foreword chapter Path

 path-combine and path-filename were bound as builtins with no emitter,
 and the whole time both already existed for real: path-filename is
 written in Foreword chapter Path, and path-combine is path-join wearing
 a name nothing implemented.

 The bindings were not merely dead. They were harmful. A program that
 never cited Path still type-checked, because the type environment
 vouched for the name, and then died at emit with a diagnostic about an
 unresolved function offset. Removing them means the same program now
 fails at name resolution, which is where it should have failed, and a
 program that does cite Path gets the function that was always there.

 This is that program.

Section: Body
  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (path-join "/src" "main.codex")
    print-line-uni (path-filename "/src/main.codex")
    print-line-uni (path-stem "/src/main.codex")
    print-line-uni (path-extension "/src/main.codex")
  end
